Caching
What is Caching?

Caching stores frequently accessed data in memory so that applications do not repeatedly fetch data from a database.
-------------------------------------------
Architecture
Request
   ↓
Redis Cache
   ↓
Database (Cache Miss)
-------------------------------------------
Cache Types

L1 Cache
--------

Local JVM Cache

Examples:

Hibernate First Level Cache

L2 Cache
--------

Shared Cache

Examples:

EhCache
Hazelcast

Distributed Cache
----------------

Shared across multiple microservices

Examples:

Redis
Memcached

Advantages
Reduced database load
Faster response time
Better throughput
Reduced application cost
Banking Examples
Customer profile data
Currency exchange rates
Product catalog information
Session data
Interview Answer

"Redis is widely used in microservices because it stores data in memory, offers sub-millisecond latency, and supports distributed caching."
